    "text": "Let <math><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> be a function such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, for all <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munderover><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></munderover><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math>. Then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munderover><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>10</mn><mn>50</mn></munderover><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;is",
